  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This paper presents a distributed data governance architecture for smart cities that combines a unified registration standard, a probe-driven dynamic catalog, and local Large Language Models (LLMs) for semantic coordination. The system was deployed in Suining City, China, connecting 151 systems across 50 departments. In a load test of 83,909 simulated requests, the platform achieved an average response time of 730 ms, a maximum latency of 1,443 ms, and an error rate of 0.12%.",
      "why": "It demonstrates a viable architecture for cross-departmental data sharing that respects ownership boundaries by restricting LLMs to semantic interpretation while using deterministic policy engines and human review to enforce security and compliance."
